00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:13.623
Okay.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:15.723
Lawrence.

00:00:15.723 --> 00:00:16.556
- Yes, sir.

00:00:16.556 --> 00:00:17.450
- [Mark] So where are you from originally?

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.450
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.550
- I grew up in Charleston, South Carolina.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:26.040
It's where I graduated high
school, went to college,

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.930
played football, all that fun stuff.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.810
- [Mark] And you grew up
with both your parents?

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.520
- Yes, sir. Yeah, my mom...

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.340
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.870
- It was pretty good for the most part.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.930
I originally lived in
Columbia, South Carolina,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.730
which is like 100 miles away,

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.500
and that's where I went to middle school,

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.270
and I shifted over to Charleston,

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.880
and it's when I first realized, you know,

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.580
like what a beach was for the most part

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.860
and man-made beaches as well.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:56.839
It was very cool.

00:00:56.839 --> 00:00:57.672
- [Mark] Is that right?

00:00:57.672 --> 00:00:58.505
- Yeah.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.003
- [Mark] Your childhood was cool?

00:01:01.003 --> 00:01:02.760
Everything was great? You
got along with both parents?

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.303
- Yes, sir. Yeah, yeah.

00:01:04.303 --> 00:01:06.060
My dad worked a lot.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:11.030
He would work late, late
shifts, so he never really

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:14.950
got a chance to go to most
of the football games,

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.863
but I mean he was there, he'd make it.

00:01:17.742 --> 00:01:21.213
- [Mark] And what age were
you when you left home?

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.030
- Oh you know, I was what 17, turning 18.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:26.863
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:01:26.863 --> 00:01:27.696
- So something like that.

00:01:27.696 --> 00:01:28.710
- [Mark] Where'd you go?

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.320
- I moved into a friend's house.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.000
He was, he had a full-time
job, his own vehicle,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.870
and his own apartment.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:39.860
And so I went from crashing at his pad

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:44.860
to paying him some cash
to live there, you know.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.380
I'd give him like 200 bucks a month.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.830
I didn't really know
like, the true meaning of,

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:54.334
you know, taking care of myself, you know.

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:57.240
So I didn't hold up then to my bargain

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.360
and it wasn't until we all
started hanging out together

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:04.527
and came together as like a
crew, we'd help each other out.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.058
- [Mark] And so you got
to LA at what point?

00:02:10.058 --> 00:02:13.133
- Man, I moved out of here fuckin' 2005,

00:02:14.639 --> 00:02:18.056
six, seven, 2000, 2000 and what 10, yeah.

00:02:21.495 --> 00:02:25.240
- [Mark] And are you living
out here on skid row right now?

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.073
- Yes, sir.

00:02:26.073 --> 00:02:26.906
- [Mark] You're in a tent?

00:02:26.906 --> 00:02:28.280
Yeah, I've been here
for fuckin' like seven,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:29.220
six, seven years.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.053
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:02:30.053 --> 00:02:30.962
Yes, sir.

00:02:30.962 --> 00:02:33.830
- [Mark] What, what's your,
what's your drug out here?

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:35.880
- Man, I like a little bit of everything.

00:02:36.818 --> 00:02:41.370
LA's notorious for their
crys, but I don't know,

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:45.707
the weed shops have, they have everything,

00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:46.740
you know, from everywhere.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:50.220
So that's a really good
choice. I don't know.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.690
I don't really mess around
with any of the other stuff

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:59.390
around here. It's kind of bogus
or it's difficult to find.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:02.412
- [Mark] So your main drug is what?

00:03:02.412 --> 00:03:05.150
- Crys, yeah probably Crys.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.430
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.890
- Well, every, everybody does it.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:12.190
It's, and nobody frowns upon it, so.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.163
- [Mark] You still, are
you still in contact

00:03:14.163 --> 00:03:14.996
with your family?

00:03:14.996 --> 00:03:16.230
- From time to time.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.730
Yeah, we've actually grown to spread apart

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:23.700
this last two years or so,

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.110
has been kind of extremely distant.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:31.210
I've contacted them
only a handful of times.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:35.650
I don't know. For some
reason, I don't know.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:36.750
This, it's yeah.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.723
These past two years have
been kind of distance.

00:03:40.598 --> 00:03:43.360
- [Mark] But, do, do you
have any kids of your own?

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.310
- Yeah, yeah. I have a newborn.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:47.143
- [Mark] You have one child?

00:03:47.143 --> 00:03:48.320
- Yeah.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.000
- [Mark] Where is he or she?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.510
- She's, she's with her mom and

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.313
they, they live here in LA.

00:03:55.509 --> 00:03:57.214
- [Mark] Do you see her?
Are you in her life?

00:03:57.214 --> 00:03:59.842
- No, I'm not in contact with them.

00:03:59.842 --> 00:04:00.717
- [Mark] No?

00:04:00.717 --> 00:04:01.550
- Huh uh, we,

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:10.230
you know, I kinda like,
I've lost contact with them,

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:12.690
I guess, you know.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.950
And I haven't, I haven't
talked to my family either

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:19.133
and I'm sure they don't
have anything to say, so.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.283
I don't.

00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:22.493
- [Mark] what are you doing for money now?

00:04:22.493 --> 00:04:24.570
- I don't have any money right now.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:28.420
I've, I just got all my
money stolen from me.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:33.008
Somebody tapped into my EBT
card as soon as I got it

00:04:33.008 --> 00:04:37.070
and took all my cash and my card.

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.870
And they said up at the
office I have to file

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:44.870
a claim, police report and
nine out of 10 times that they,

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:51.010
even if they do pursue, that
I'm only gonna get my cash.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.573
And that's, you know, it's,
it's not, it's still not,

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.583
it's not fair.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.470
- [Mark] Yeah. Bad stuff
happens here a lot.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:05.420
- If they pursue and most
of the time they don't.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:10.143
So, no, it's just, it's pretty sure...

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.063
- [Mark] But in general,
what do you do for money?

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:19.570
- It's extremely difficult
to get work around here.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.670
Recycling, fortunate enough for me

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:27.530
I know the late night recyclers,

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:30.612
so that if I miss in the morning time,

00:05:30.612 --> 00:05:33.040
that I can go at night and cash out

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.143
and still have money to
get something to eat.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:41.580
But even that is extremely difficult

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.630
in competition with everybody else, like,

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.500
and then when you, when
you go to pick cans,

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:50.650
everybody, they nowadays we
leave the cans, the, the doors

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:55.650
to the trash cans open, so
that the next person can see.

00:05:55.779 --> 00:05:56.612
- [Mark] Right.

00:05:56.612 --> 00:06:00.240
- You know and you see
one trash can fucked up

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.793
and there goes your route for the night,

00:06:04.104 --> 00:06:06.760
because he's one step ahead of you.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:07.970
- [Mark] Oh, I see.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.553
- Just, yeah man, that shit happens, so.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:17.490
Usually I would walk from
downtown to MacArthur Park

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.860
and between downtown and MacArthur Park

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:25.860
I would collect averagely
speaking $10 worth of cans.

00:06:28.424 --> 00:06:31.830
And it's just enough.
It fills up everything.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.993
One whole cart, maximum it's 10 bucks.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:38.410
- [Mark] Yeah. How old are you?

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.133
- I'm 30. I'm about to be 31 in January.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:44.174
- [Mark] Do you have any plans?

00:06:44.174 --> 00:06:48.263
I had, I had plans.

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:54.550
Honestly, since, since everything happened

00:06:56.559 --> 00:06:59.203
and it being extremely
difficult to find work,

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:06.420
I've been living life,
the maximum bum status.

00:07:09.171 --> 00:07:11.953
Just, not that I don't give a fuck,

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:18.390
but I'm absolutely not wasting any effort

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:22.703
on anything until it's time.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.530
And at that point, then
I'll take a step forward

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:30.703
in the right direction,
whatever direction that is.

00:07:30.703 --> 00:07:31.536
- [Mark] Right.

00:07:31.536 --> 00:07:33.700
- But until then, nah dud, like,

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:38.560
I'm not going on a crazy
mission, side missions,

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.120
gonna be a redirected, misinterpreted.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.820
I'm just gonna sit back and chill.

00:07:44.882 --> 00:07:47.390
(indistinct)

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:48.820
- [Mark] Well, Lawrence, thank
you so much for talking me.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:49.653
- Yeah man, for sure.

00:07:49.653 --> 00:07:51.080
- [Mark] Good luck with
everything out there.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:51.913
- All right.

00:07:51.913 --> 00:07:52.746
- [Mark] Be careful.

00:07:52.746 --> 00:07:54.210
- Thank you, thank you. You do the same.

